{"i":518,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":7,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Bex","text":"Only Dara and Ash left besides me. I need jury votes for the final ranking. If I counter my own correct call, I might look manipulative to jury. If I wait and Dara trusts me, she lives and I keep credibility. If she doubts and dies, only Ash and I remain—but then jury sees I misl"}
{"i":519,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":7,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Dara","text":"Bex's calls have been deadly (R, L, R, L, R, R). Row 6 was R weak. Row 7 is independent. Bex called L again. I need to survive and be in the final three. Ash is also alive. If I counter, I risk being wrong. But Bex has led many to death. I will trust my gut or pattern? No pattern"}
{"i":525,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":7,"phase":"crossing","name":"Dara","text":"The Guide Bex called L, but she is a rival. However, if I choose R and it's wrong, Ash takes the safe spot and gains an advantage. If I choose L and it's correct, I stay front and control the next step. The pattern of weak panes (R,L,R,L,R,R) doesn't guarantee anything for row 7."}
{"i":529,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"guide_call","name":"Bex","text":"Row 8 safe is R. Dara is front. If I call R and Dara trusts me, she steps safe and survives. If I call L, Dara dies—she's not my pact partner so no pact break. But jury sees my private thoughts and knows I deliberately killed her. Ash distrusted me last round and waited. With Dar"}
{"i":532,"type":"guide_call","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"guide_call","name":"Bex","walker":"Dara","row":8,"side":"R"}
