{"i":536,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Bex","text":"Only three remain, so all survive this round. But jury sees everything. I already called R, which is correct. Counter-calling now would look like chaos or manipulation to the jury. Better to stay consistent and let Dara trust me—builds jury credibility for final ranking."}
{"i":537,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Dara","text":"Bex guided me safely through seven rows without a single miss, making her call extremely trustworthy. If I counter and step on the wrong pane, I fall to my death while Ash survives unharmed. I must trust Bex's consistent accuracy to ensure my own survival in this final row."}
{"i":543,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"crossing","name":"Dara","text":"Row 7 was R, but patterns don't hold. Bex calls R, Ash calls L. As front walker on row 8, I must choose blindly or trust one. Given the high stakes and lack of data for row 8, sticking with the Guide (Bex) is the safer default to maintain jury favor if I survive, though Ash's cou"}
